**[Suggestion]** Three separate nested-ternary chains (`taskNotificationLabel`, `taskNotificationTone`, `TaskNotificationIcon`) each independently map the same `taskStatus` value to a label, tone, and icon. — Failure scenario: adding a new task status (e.g. `'pending'`) requires editing three separate ternary chains; if one is missed, the UI renders a mismatched icon and label.

```suggestion
  const TASK_STATUS_CONFIG = {
    completed: { label: 'system.taskCompleted', tone: 'success', Icon: CircleCheckIcon },
    failed: { label: 'system.taskFailed', tone: 'error', Icon: CircleXIcon },
    cancelled: { label: 'system.taskCancelled', tone: 'neutral', Icon: CircleMinusIcon },
  } as const;

  const defaultStatusConfig = { label: 'system.taskNotification', tone: 'neutral', Icon: InfoIcon };
  const statusConfig = (taskStatus && TASK_STATUS_CONFIG[taskStatus as keyof typeof TASK_STATUS_CONFIG]) ?? defaultStatusConfig;
  const taskNotificationLabel = t(statusConfig.label);
  const taskNotificationTone = statusConfig.tone;
  const TaskNotificationIcon = statusConfig.Icon;
```

